ArchiMate Model Exchange File Format — vendored XSDs
=====================================================

Source: The Open Group, ArchiMate Model Exchange File Format
Index page: https://www.opengroup.org/xsd/archimate/

Files vendored verbatim:
  archimate3_Model.xsd     https://www.opengroup.org/xsd/archimate/3.1/archimate3_Model.xsd
  archimate3_View.xsd      https://www.opengroup.org/xsd/archimate/3.1/archimate3_View.xsd
  archimate3_Diagram.xsd   https://www.opengroup.org/xsd/archimate/3.1/archimate3_Diagram.xsd

Schema version: 3.1
Specification: covers ArchiMate 3.1 and ArchiMate 3.2 (no breaking changes to the
               exchange format between 3.1 and 3.2; The Open Group publishes one
               XSD set under the 3.1 path that serves both).
Retrieval date: 2026-05-27

Companion publication (the Guide): https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/archimate31-exchange-file-format-guide/

These files are vendored unmodified. Do not edit. To update, replace verbatim
from the source URLs and bump the retrieval date.

The XSDs themselves do not embed a redistribution license. The Open Group hosts
them publicly under the URL above for use by ArchiMate tooling implementers.

ArchiMate 3.2 relationship matrix
---------------------------------

The XSDs above do not encode the per-(source, relation, target) triple matrix
from the ArchiMate specification. That matrix is vendored from the Archi
modelling tool (https://www.archimatetool.com/), which ships it in
machine-readable form. Archi is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE-archi.txt.

Files vendored verbatim from
https://github.com/archimatetool/archi (Archi v5.9.0, commit a43b626, 2026-05-19):

  relationships.xml        com.archimatetool.model/model/relationships.xml
  relationships-keys.xml   com.archimatetool.model/model/relationships-keys.xml

The matrix is version-tagged 3.2 inside the file. The generator parses both
files to validate (source-kind, relation, target-kind) triples in artifacts.
